{"step_index":238,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-17T14:48:58Z","thinking":"**Initiating Design Documentation**\n\nI'm starting to create the `design.md` file. My objective is to produce a detailed System Design Document, suitable for production, while embodying the roles of both a Principal Systems Architect and a Principal PM. I will ensure thoroughness.\n\n\n**Defining System Structure**\n\nI've outlined the major sections for the System Design Document, focusing on the HR agentic solution's MVP 1. Specifically, I'm fleshing out the context and objectives, ensuring that architectural principles like Zero-Trust and Loose Coupling are clearly defined. I'm also mapping out the high-level architecture and component decomposition into layers: Client, Gateway, Core Agent Platform, Knowledge & Retrieval, Integration Adapters, and Resilience. I need to get started on the data architecture next.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":"{\"RequestFeedback\":false,\"Summary\":\"Comprehensive System Design Document (design.md) for the HR Agentic Solution (MVP 1).\",\"UserFacing\":true}","CodeContent":"\"# System Design Document: HR Agentic Solution (MVP 1)\\n\\n**Document Version:** 1.0.0  \\n**Status:** Approved / Ready for Implementation  \\n**Authors:** Principal Systems Architect & Principal Product Manager  \\n**Target Release:** MVP 1.0 (Q3 2026)  \\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Executive Summary & Design Principles\\n\\nThe **HR Agentic Solution** is an enterprise-grade virtual assistant platform designed to automate Tier-1 HR/IT policy inquiries and execute self-service transactional workflows across **WorkWeek (HCM)** and **ServiceImmediately (ITSM/HRSD)**.\\n\\n```mermaid\\ngraph LR\\n    User([Employee]) --> UI[Web Chat UI]\\n    UI --> Gateway[API Gateway & Auth Proxy]\\n    Gateway --> Safety[Safety & Guardrails]\\n    Safety --> Orchestrator[Agent Orchestrator]\\n    Orchestrator --> RAG[(Policy Vector DB)]\\n    Orchestrator --> WW[WorkWeek Adapter]\\n    Orchestrator --> SI[ServiceImmediately Adapter]\\n    Orchestrator --> DLQ[(HR Ops DLQ)]\\n```\\n\\n### Core Architectural Principles\\n\\n1. **Zero-Trust Identity Assertion:** Even in the MVP 1 test-credential sandbox environment, all user turns are authenticated via an **API Gateway Mock Identity Assertion Layer** that injects a cryptographically signed JWT (`X-Authenticated-User`) to enforce strict Role-Based Access Control (RBAC).\\n2. **Deterministic State Mutation via Human-in-the-Loop (HITL):** The autonomous LLM is strictly prohibited from mutating external backend state without rendering an interactive **Confirmation Card** for explicit user review and authorization.\\n3. **Resilience & Forward SAGA Consistency:** Multi-system chained workflows avoid brittle two-phase rollbacks; instead, they preserve successful upstream state and route partial downstream failures to an **HR Operations Dead-Letter Queue (DLQ)** with transparent user notifications.\\n4. **Defense-in-Depth AI Safety:** Input guardrails, domain containment, closed-domain RAG retrieval gating, and NER-based SPII masking guarantee $\\\\ge 99.5\\\\%$ safety precision/recall and 0% ungrounded policy hallucinations.\\n\\n--\n<truncated 18895 bytes>","Description":"\"Create system design document design.md in artifact directory\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"/usr/local/google/home/gauravrawat/.gemini/jetski/brain/ca4322d4-9341-4bd7-ad62-33640faaced0/design.md\"","toolAction":"\"Writing design.md to artifact directory\"","toolSummary":"\"Write design.md artifact\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
