{"step_index":256,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-17T14:52:27Z","thinking":"**Defining the Architecture**\n\nOkay, I'm now zeroing in on the System Design Document, specifically the `design.md` file. I've pinpointed that the user is requesting a GCP-centric architectural blueprint. The focus is to articulate the architecture and map the full solution based on the user's requirements.\n\n\n**Mapping the System Components**\n\nI'm now detailing the system components within the Google Cloud ecosystem. The breakdown includes: the client-side technologies, such as Cloud Run, Cloud Storage with Cloud CDN or Firebase Hosting for the Web Chat UI; and SSE or WebSocket streaming through Cloud Run. The ingress, gateway, and auth tier leverages Google Cloud API Gateway or Apigee, plus Cloud Load Balancing and Cloud Armor. Finally, I'm mapping AI safety guardrails using Vertex AI Model Armor and Content Safety, along with Cloud DLP for security.\n\n\n**Detailing the Architecture Components**\n\nI'm now diving into the specifics of service accounts for least-privilege access across tiers. I'm also fleshing out the Agent Orchestrator, which could use Vertex AI Agent Builder, LangGraph, or Cloud Run/GKE. For foundation models, I'm leaning toward Gemini 1.5 Pro/Flash on Vertex AI, and Memorystore for Redis will handle session state. Moreover, for the Policy Knowledge Base, I'm planning to ingest documents via Cloud Storage with a Pub/Sub notification pipeline using Eventarc, Cloud Functions or Cloud Run. The documents will be processed via Document AI, with vector embeddings from the Vertex AI Text Embedding API, and the Vertex AI Vector Search for retrieval.\n\n\n**Integrating the Adapters**\n\nI've been working on integrating specific system adapters. Specifically, the WorkWeek HCM and ServiceImmediately ITSM adapters are being deployed as Cloud Run microservices. They're using VPC Access Connector for secure egress. Google Cloud Secret Manager will handle secrets and API keys, and I'm considering Envoy, Resilience4j, or a custom Go circuit breaker for resilience.\n\n\\n\\n\n\n**Managing Resilience and Queues**\n\nNow, I'm focusing on resilience, messaging, and asynchronous dead-letter queues. I'm leveraging Cloud Pub/Sub, specifically the `hr-ops-dlq-topic` for dead-letter queue events. An HR Operations Notification Cloud Function will subscribe to this and integrate with PagerDuty, Slack, or HRSD. I'm also planning to use Cloud Tasks for reliable asynchronous task execution and exponential backoff retry handling.\n\n\\n\\n\n\n**Establishing Observability and Auditing**\n\nFinally, I'm establishing the observability, governance, and audit logging components. The primary audit database will be Cloud SQL for PostgreSQL, with CMEK, IAM database authentication, and a private IP in the VPC. For monitoring and tracing, I'm using Cloud Logging, Cloud Monitoring, and Cloud Trace, considering OpenTelemetry or Sherlog for distributed tracing.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":"{\"RequestFeedback\":false,\"Summary\":\"Comprehensive Google Cloud Platform (GCP) System Design Document (design.md) for the HR Agentic Solution (MVP 1).\",\"UserFacing\":true}","CodeContent":"\"# System Design Document: HR Agentic Solution (GCP Architecture)\\n\\n**Document Version:** 2.0.0 (Google Cloud Platform Edition)  \\n**Target Platform:** Google Cloud Platform (GCP)  \\n**Target LLM:** Google Gemini 1.5 Pro / Flash via Vertex AI  \\n**Authors:** Principal Systems Architect & Principal Product Manager  \\n**Status:** Approved / Ready for Implementation  \\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Executive Summary & GCP Architectural Principles\\n\\nThe **HR Agentic Solution** is an enterprise AI-driven virtual assistant deployed natively on **Google Cloud Platform (GCP)**. The platform orchestrates complex, multi-turn HR and IT self-service workflows across **WorkWeek (HCM)**, **ServiceImmediately (ITSM/HRSD)**, and internal policy repositories.\\n\\n```mermaid\\ngraph LR\\n    User([Employee]) --> LB[Cloud Load Balancing + Cloud Armor]\\n    LB --> Gateway[API Gateway / Cloud Run]\\n    Gateway --> Guard[Vertex Model Armor & Cloud DLP]\\n    Guard --> Orchestrator[Agent on Cloud Run / Vertex AI]\\n    Orchestrator --> Gemini[Gemini 1.5 on Vertex AI]\\n    Orchestrator --> VectorSearch[(Vertex AI Vector Search)]\\n    Orchestrator --> Adapters[Adapters on Cloud Run]\\n    Orchestrator --> DLQ[(Cloud Pub/Sub DLQ)]\\n```\\n\\n### Core GCP Design Tenets\\n\\n1. **Serverless-First & Elastic Scale:** All compute workloads (Chat UI, API Gateway, Agent Orchestrator, Integration Adapters) run on **Cloud Run** with automated scale-to-zero and sub-second scale-up.\\n2. **Managed Enterprise AI via Vertex AI:** Leveraging **Gemini 1.5 Pro/Flash** with structured function calling, **Vertex AI Vector Search** for sub-millisecond semantic retrieval, and **Vertex AI Model Armor** for prompt injection defense.\\n3. **Zero-Trust Identity with Cloud KMS:** Ingress traffic passes through an **API Gateway Mock Identity Assertion Layer** that cryptographically signs JWT session claims (`X-Authenticated-User`) using asymmetric keys in **Cloud KMS**.\\n4. **Data Privacy via Sensitive Data Protection (Cloud DLP):** Real-time inspection and automated tokenization/redaction\n<truncated 21115 bytes>","Description":"\"Create GCP System Design Document design.md in artifact directory\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"/usr/local/google/home/gauravrawat/.gemini/jetski/brain/ca4322d4-9341-4bd7-ad62-33640faaced0/design.md\"","toolAction":"\"Writing GCP design.md to artifact directory\"","toolSummary":"\"Write GCP design.md artifact\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
