{"step_index":276,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-17T14:56:37Z","content":"The **System Design Document (`design.md`)** has been customized and architected natively for **Google Cloud Platform (GCP)**:\n\n* 📄 **Markdown File (Direct Local Artifact):** [design.md](file:///usr/local/google/home/gauravrawat/.gemini/jetski/brain/ca4322d4-9341-4bd7-ad62-33640faaced0/design.md)\n* 📁 **Workspace Copy:** [design.md](file:///google/src/cloud/gauravrawat/summarize_latest_chats/google3/hr_agentic_solution/design.md)\n* 🔗 **Google Docs Link:** [HR Agentic Solution - System Design Document (GCP Edition)](https://docs.google.com/document/d/1L9fEz7mnPjSDlVHkUB4AKconIcoNZGoY8m6ZA5qtkGs/edit)\n* 📂 **Google Drive Project Folder:** [HR Agentic Solution - Project Artifacts](https://drive.google.com/corp/drive/folders/115mF5i6YL6YdECFDMdHJoO5gYTXVxEvl)\n\n---\n\n### Google Cloud Platform (GCP) Technology Stack & Mapping\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                                GCP NATIVE SERVICE MAPPING MATRIX                                │\n├───────────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────┤\n│ Architecture Layer            │ Google Cloud Service / Component │ Core Responsibility          │\n├───────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────┤\n│ 1. Edge Ingress & WAF         │ Cloud Load Balancing             │ Global Anycast HTTPS \n<truncated 3528 bytes>\n───────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────┤\n│ 8. Audit & Observability      │ Cloud SQL for PostgreSQL (CMEK)  │ Immutable Audit Database     │\n│                               │ Cloud Logging / Trace (APM)      │ OpenTelemetry Trace Logs     │\n├───────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────┤\n│ 9. Infrastructure as Code     │ HashiCorp Terraform              │ Declarative GCP Blueprint    │\n└───────────────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n### Highlights of the GCP Design Specification:\n1. **Serverless Scalability on Cloud Run:** Automatic scale-to-zero during non-business hours and instantaneous scaling to absorb company-wide open enrollment surges.\n2. **Sub-10ms Vector Retrieval with Vertex AI Vector Search:** ScaNN-powered index with metadata filtering on document version and policy category.\n3. **Automated Sensitive Data Protection (Cloud DLP):** Integrated de-identification pipeline masking SSNs, phone numbers, and home addresses before logs touch Cloud SQL.\n4. **Resilient Forward SAGA with Cloud Pub/Sub:** Partial orchestration failures in chained flows (UC-2.2) trigger events to the `hr-ops-dead-letter-topic` for manual HR Operations resolution without data rollback.\n5. **Production Terraform Blueprint:** Complete IaC code defining GCS buckets, Vertex Vector Search indexes, Memorystore Redis, Pub/Sub topics, and Cloud Run service definitions.","truncated_fields":["content"]}
{"step_index":277,"source":"USER_EXPLICIT","type":"USER_INPUT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-17T16:14:24Z","content":"<USER_REQUEST>\n\n\nYour objective is to critically analyze, stress-test, and find gaps in the following business requirements / PRD before implementation begins.\n\n---\n### Input Requirements\nHR Agentic Solution BRD (MVP 1 - Revised & Approved)\n---\n\n### Analysis Framework\nEvaluate the requirements and organize your analysis into the following structured sections:\n\n#### 1. Clarity & Ambiguity Check\n- Identify all vague, subjective, or underspecified statements (e.g., \"fast response\", \"seamless experience\", \"support high traffic\").\n- Point out contradictory requirements or terms with ambiguous definitions.\n\n#### 2. Missing Functional Scope & Edge Cases\nIdentify unhandled scenarios, including:\n- **State & Lifecycle:** Missing status transitions, lifecycle edge cases (e.g., cancellations, retries, expired states).\n- **Boundary & Input Extremes:** Empty states, maximum limits, duplicate submissions, special characters/formats.\n- **Permission & Multi-tenancy:** Unauthorized access attempts, cross-tenant leaks, role edge cases.\n- **Failures & Degradation:** Network drops, timeout handling, partial failures, third-party dependency outages.\n\n#### 3. Non-Functional Requirements (NFR) Assessment\nReview and highlight missing or unrealistic constraints:\n- **Performance & Scale:** Expected throughput (QPS), latency targets (p50/p95/p99), and data growth.\n- **Reliability & Availability:** Uptime targets (SLO/SLA), disaster recovery, data consistency requirements.\n- **Security & Compliance:** PII handling, data encryption, RBAC, audit logging, regulatory needs (GDPR, HIPAA, SOC2).\n\n#### 4. System Dependencies & Technical Risks\n- Identify implicit dependencies on upstream/downstream services or legacy systems.\n- Highlight architectural bottlenecks, data migration complexities, or integration risks.\n\n#### 5. Scope Creep & Feasibility (MoSCoW)\n- Categorize requirements into **Must-Have**, **Should-Have**, **Could-Have**, and **Won't-Have (v1)**.\n- Suggest items that can be deferred to a later phase to reduce launch risk.\n\n#### 6. Clarifying Questions & Action Items\n- Provide a prioritized list of specific questions for stakeholders/product owners to unblock engineering.\n- Provide 3–5 sample acceptance criteria written in Given-When-Then (Gherkin) format for the core flows.\n</USER_REQUEST>\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\nThe user is: gauravrawat.\nThe current local time is: 2026-08-17T16:14:24Z.\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>"}
